## WHY HE "CANNOT GET BACK THERE" (DERIVED by reading at the base; not run in a browser, no hosted call was made)
1. The only logo links to the page are on the three sign-in renders: `ApprovalLogoLink.tsx:12` (path const `:10`), used at `UatStartScreen.tsx:73` and `SignInScreen.tsx:56` and `:126`. A visitor who already holds a level never sees them: `UatStartScreen.tsx:65` and `SignInScreen.tsx:51` / `:118` send a signed-in visitor straight on to their level's start page. The logo inside the app goes to `/workspace` (`AppShell.tsx:160`), not to the page.
2. For a visitor with no level the link is followed into the sign-in gate: `proxy.ts:84` (`auth.kind === "uat"` needs a level) and `:110` redirect to `/?next=...`, the same start screen (the laptop's mock does the same in `AppShell.tsx:80`), so it looks as if nothing happened.
3. After choosing a level that is not Admin the page loads and then fails: the list call is Admin-only (`FeedbackModule.cs:166` with the policy at `:103`), the page says "Only the Admin role can review feedback." (`FeedbackReview.tsx:22`, used `:45` and `:64`).
4. On UAT and the demo, Delete is refused for every level before sign-in: `FeedbackModule.cs:171` carries `.Destructive()`, and `UatOpenAuthentication.cs:192-200` answers 403 `uat.action-off` (the page keeps the item and says the service error, `FeedbackReview.tsx:64`; pinned by `FeedbackReview.test.tsx:166`).

