## THE DESIGN (property first; D-1 to D-5 are accepted unless slot S10 changes them)
**Property:** in the review-copy modes (the web's `auth.kind === "uat"`: UAT and the demo, the only modes where an open sign-in exists) and on the laptop's mock, a visitor with NO session, and a visitor at EACH of the four levels, can (a) open `/admin/feedback/review` (exactly that path), (b) read the held items, (c) approve one, (d) delete one; everything else about who can do what is byte-for-byte what it is at the base. In the Entra (hosted production) mode nothing changes at all (a signed-out visitor is still sent to sign in; D-3).
- **D-1 (where the door is): in the WEB layer, not the API.** The API keeps its Admin policy (`FeedbackModule.cs:103`, `:166`, `:169`, `:171`) so "Admin 200, others 403, signed-out 401" at the API stays true (`ReviewHeldTests.cs:223-229`; reach tables `UatOpenTests.cs:511-514`, `UatOpenDemoTests.cs:235`; the deploy seats probe it). The web BFF (`bff.ts`, the 401 at `:432-441` and the assertion at `:439`) mints the **admin-level assertion** for exactly THREE operations, whatever level or no level the visitor holds: (1) `GET /api/v1/feedback` whose query is exactly `state=held` plus optionally `limit` (nothing else: no `category`, no other state); (2) `POST /api/v1/feedback/{id}/submit`; (3) `DELETE /api/v1/feedback/{id}`, `{id}` matching the id shape the API uses (read it). Match on the path AFTER `routedPath` (`bff.ts:189`, the same normaliser the router uses: case and percent-encoding), and on the method; a path that is not exactly one of the three is the visitor's own level or 401 as today. The attachment download (`FeedbackModule.cs:167`) and the list without `state=held` (the "Feedback received" page's call) are NOT opened. Alternative (API made anonymous, `AllowAnonymous` on the three routes) is NOT built: it would open the Internet-facing API host in every mode and break the Admin-only probe; if you find the web layer cannot do it, `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY D-1`.
- **D-2 (the page without a session):** `proxy.ts:79-86` `needsSignIn` returns false for the path `/admin/feedback/review` (exact, with or without one trailing slash, no prefix match) when `auth.kind === "uat"`; the client shell lets that one path render with no user in the `uat` and `mock` modes (`AppShell.tsx:78-83` redirect and `:99` loading state), showing the page in a bare main (no navigation, no account button, no new element or word); every other path redirects as before. A signed-in visitor sees the page in the normal shell, as today. If the shell cannot do it without a new word or element, a second `(group)` layout holding only the page is allowed (same URL; the test that imports the page, `FeedbackReview.test.tsx:9`, follows it).
- **D-3 (production is untouched):** with `auth.kind` of `entra` or `off`, `needsSignIn`, the BFF 401 (`bff.ts:416-429`) and the shell redirect are byte-for-byte as before. No new setting, no new environment variable, no new header.
- **D-4 (Delete on the review copies):** remove `.Destructive()` from the deleteFeedback route ONLY (`FeedbackModule.cs:171`), so "dismiss" works on UAT and the demo; reset demo (`AssessmentModule.cs:230`), personal-data export and erase (`:232`, `:233`) keep it. Update the route-table pins that list deleteFeedback as destructive (`UatOpenTests.cs:551` and `:621`; read the surrounding classification test and its `SoftNames`, moving the name to the soft list WITH the reason: "erases one held item the product owner's 13:08 ruling opens to anyone on the review copies", and the text "five destructive actions" wherever it counts them). The page's text, button names and confirm sentence do not change (no new word).
- **D-5 (who is recorded):** the audit actor of an approve or delete is the review copy's fixed Admin identity, as the code gives it (`FeedbackReviewEndpoints.cs:39`, `:73`); no visitor identity is added, no new field, no new header. State this in STATUS.
- **Same-origin / CSRF stays:** every mutation passes `guard()` (`guard.ts:49`, called at `bff.ts:403` BEFORE the auth branch) so a cross-site or cross-origin POST or DELETE with no session is 403 and never reaches the minting line. Rate limits: the API's per-user limiter covers submitting new feedback only (`FeedbackModule.cs:165`); approve and delete have none today and act through one conditional UPDATE (409 when not held, `FeedbackReviewEndpoints.cs:45-62`); judge: add none (no pattern to follow), and say so in STATUS.

## EVERY OTHER ADMIN-ONLY SURFACE KEEPS ITS RESTRICTION (property; "at least these", then "any other shape: prove it meets the property or STOP")
